      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T12:23:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks both of you.\n\nPer discussed with mark, using \"dumpsys ethernet\" to check available tethering interface on T+ device because there is no api to get iface\u0027s NetworkCapabilities (for testPhysicalEthernet problem mentioned) and \"waiting X seconds approach\" has the above concern (slow down test) as the following try which takes 5+ sec to complete the test (timeout 5s).\n\nlog:\n[1/10] android.net.EthernetTetheringTest#testIcmpv6Echo: PASSED (5.259s)\n\nsrc:\n```\nprivate boolean isInterfaceForTetheringAvailable() throws Exception {\n    final TetheredInterfaceRequester tetheredInterfaceRequester \u003d\n            new TetheredInterfaceRequester(mHandler, mEm);\n    try {\n        tetheredInterfaceRequester.getInterface();\n        return true;\n    } catch (TimeoutException e) {\n         return false;\n    } finally {\n        runAsShell(NETWORK_SETTINGS, () -\u003e\n            tetheredInterfaceRequester.release());            \n    }\n```",
